<title>SINGAPORE: SINGAPORE BUNKERS OFFERED $3/T HIGHER.</title>
<headline>SINGAPORE BUNKERS OFFERED $3/T HIGHER.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore bunkers were offered sharply higher amid firmer cargo and rising swap prices, traders said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>They said 380-cst sellers were at $107/$109 per tonne and 180-cst was offered at around $110-112--both up $3 from Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Everybody's pulling up their offers because the cargo and swaps markets are going up and demand is pretty heavy,&quot; one supplier said. A 180-cst cargo traded on Tuesday at $103.50 on free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>MDO and gas oil were indicated at $168 and $178 per tonne, respectively. -- Singapore Newsroom (65-870 3093)</p>
